WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.560
One morning, BHW Marites has three tasks. She will lead a health discussion, plan with residents, and help Aling Nena contact the midwife.

2
00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:21.260
At the discussion, Marites listens to people's questions and shares clear, approved health information. This is her Health Educator role.

3
00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:30.280
For a barangay clean-up, Marites invites residents to plan and act with her. As a Community Organizer, she brings people together.

4
00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:40.020
When Aling Nena needs help for her child, Marites helps her contact the midwife. In the Health Service Provider role, she helps the family reach care.

5
00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:55.840
The Reference Manual uses the term barangay-level Health Education and Promotion Officer, or HEPO. Teaching, organizing, and service support connect in this role; the diagram does not prove a formal appointment.

6
00:00:56.140 --> 00:01:10.140
Before sharing information, Marites learns the barangay's priorities and confirms uncertain details with a health worker. Remember: educate, connect people, and guide them to services with accurate knowledge.
